---
// refunds.astro - Refund Policy: a DRAFT for the owner's review. Refunds go
// through Paddle, never by email to us: nothing may depend on a person
// answering mail. The legal details come from src/data/legal.ts.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import LegalValue from '../components/legal/LegalValue.astro';
import { REFUND_DAYS, getPlan } from '../data/plans';

const bee = getPlan('bee');
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Refund Policy"
  description={`A full refund of any HivePaaS license payment on request within ${REFUND_DAYS} days, through Paddle, our merchant of record.`}
  path="/refunds"
>
  <h2 id="policy">A full refund within {REFUND_DAYS} days</h2>
  <p>
    If HivePaaS is not right for you, any payment for a license is refunded in full on request within{' '}
    {REFUND_DAYS} days of the payment. That holds for the first payment and for every renewal, monthly or yearly. You
    do not need to give a reason.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how">How to ask for a refund</h2>
  <p>
    Paddle.com is our merchant of record: it sold you the license, and it handles refunds. Ask through Paddle, not by
    email to us:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Go to <a href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a>.</li>
    <li>Find your order with the email address you paid with.</li>
    <li>Ask for a refund of the payment.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The money goes back to the payment method you used. How long it takes to arrive depends on your bank or card
    provider.
  </p>

  <h2 id="after">What happens after a refund</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The license is revoked.</strong> Once a payment for a period - the first one or a renewal - is refunded
      in full, the portal issues no more keys for the license: no renewals, plan changes or moves.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The subscription is canceled.</strong> The portal cancels it at once, so nothing more is charged for it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The key you have runs out on its own.</strong> Keys are checked offline and cannot be recalled, so the
      key already installed keeps working until it runs out. The installation is then on {bee.name}, the free plan.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Nothing that runs is stopped.</strong> As at any expiry, apps, functions, users and nodes stay; only
      creating more beyond {bee.name}'s limits stops.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="other">Partial refunds and credits</h2>
  <p>
    A partial refund, a credit, or a refund of a plan change's charge does not revoke the license or cancel the
    subscription.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
  <p>
    For a payment or a refund, contact Paddle at <a href="https://paddle.net">paddle.net</a>. For anything else:{' '}
    <LegalValue field="contactEmail" />.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
